    {
      "id": "0093b6d763892a65cfa4c741824f879c109342d8",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 548858029,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> I'm open to other suggestions and criticism should this solution or the implementation of it be sub-par.\n\nThere's the user-visible side of the solution; this change can be thought of as a prototype for that (although it might be more of a prototype if something similar were done for radiotap, so that both 802.11 and 802.15.4 users saw it).\n\nThere's the implementation-level side, which requires more thought - for example, how much of it should be done in libwiretap and how much in libwireshark.  For example, It Might Be Nice if for various forms of metadata there were a standard metadata header that multiple encapsulations could share (like `struct ieee_802_11_phdr` for 802.11), filled in by libwiretap whenever possible, so that, as an example, 802.11 packets in a NetMon file, with  the NetMon radio header, could be translated into 802.11 packets in a pcap or pcapng file, with a radiotap header, using editcap (which has no dissectors and thus wouldn't itself interpret either radio header).  There are other interesting things that could be done.\n\nBut that requires more thought.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-04-10T09:16:28.337Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-04-10T09:16:28.337Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 95370867,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
